  "source": "The National Board of Health and Welfare",
  "note": [
    "Indicator definition: Number of deaths with explicit alcohol diagnosis (ICD-10: E24.4, F10, G31.2, G62.1, G72.1, I42.6, K29.2, K70, K85.2, K86.0, O35.4, P04.3, Q86.0, T51, Y90.1–Y90.9, Y91.1–Y91.9, Z50.2, Z71.4 or Z72.1) as an underlying or contributory cause of death per 100,000 inhabitants aged 15 or older. Mortality rates are age-standardised with the average national population in 2021 as the standard population. The data are presented by year and can be disaggregated by county (based on the county in which the deceased was registered at the time of death), gender and age groups."
  ]
